# CholoBD Expo — Frontend → Mobile Integration Helper

> Use this when porting or integrating a module/section from the Next.js frontend
> (`NextJS-choloBD-frontend`) into this Expo app. Mobile is a **mobile import + restyle**
> of the web app: same backend APIs and feature intent, different UI stack and data layer.
>
> Always cross-check remaining gaps in `app-integration-progress.mdc`.
> Follow mobile conventions in `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and
> `.github/instructions/*` — those take precedence over web patterns.

---

## 1. Premise

| Concern | Frontend (Next.js) | Mobile (Expo) |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js App Router + React DOM | Expo Router + React Native |
| HTTP | `apiFetch` + session cookies (`credentials: 'include'`) | Axios + JWT Bearer via `axiosClient` |
| Data hooks | TanStack Query `use*RQ` inside `*Api` files | `useFetch*` / `use*Logic` in `src/hooks/` |
| UI source of truth | `src/components/modular-components/**` | `src/components/{domain}/` + `ui/` + `interface/` |
| Pages | Thin `src/app/**/page.tsx` shells | Thin `src/app/**/*.tsx` screens (default export) |
| Styling | Tailwind + `theme-*` / CSS vars in `globals.css` | NativeWind `className` + `theme.ts` tokens |
| Auth gate | Session / parallel dashboard slots | `authSlice` + `useAuthWithAdminCheck` |
| i18n | Web i18n (if present) | **Required:** `TRANSLATION_KEYS` + `en.json` / `bn.json` |
| Dark mode | `data-theme` CSS themes | `dark:` classes + `useTheme()` |

**Rule:** Copy **behavior and API contracts** from frontend; rebuild **UI and data wiring** in mobile patterns. Do not paste web DOM/Tailwind/`use*RQ` code into RN files.

---

## 2. Layer mapping (where things go)

### 2.1 API connectors

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| `src/services/api/{domain}Api.ts` | `src/services/api/{domain}.ts` |
| Barrel `src/services/api/index.ts` (`HotelApi`, …) | **No barrel** — import the file directly |
| Private fetcher + `useGetXRQ` / `useCreateXRQ` | Named `export async function` only; hooks live separately |
| `apiFetch('/path')` → full `ApiResponse` | `getApiInstance().get/post(...)` → return **`res.data.data`** (unwrapped) |
| Cookie session auth | Bearer token (interceptor already handles it) |

**Conversion steps for an API file:**
1. Open frontend `{domain}Api.ts` and list every endpoint (method + path + body/query).
2. Create/extend `src/services/api/{domain}.ts` with matching named functions.
3. Move request/response shapes into `src/types/{domain}.ts` (do not keep interfaces only inside the API file unless the domain already does that).
4. Unwrap `{ status, message, data }` — callers get `data`, not the envelope.
5. Do **not** port React Query hooks into the service file.
6. For complex domains (tour builder, trip planner, package bookings), add a local `mapApiError` only if sibling files already use that pattern.

```ts
// Frontend pattern (do not copy as-is)
export function useGetBookingsRQ(queryString?: string) {
  return useQuery({ queryFn: () => getBookings(queryString), ... });
}

// Mobile pattern
export async function getUserBookings(params?: {...}): Promise<Booking[]> {
  const res = await getApiInstance().get('/api/bookings/hotel-rooms', { params });
  return res.data.data;
}
```

**Path note:** Mobile calls usually include the `/api` prefix on the path (or rely on `API_BASE_URL` that already ends before `/api` — match existing files like `locations.ts` / `tourBuilder.ts`).

### 2.2 Types & validators

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| Types often inline in `*Api.ts` or component files | Prefer `src/types/{domain}.ts` |
| Zod / form validation (varies) | `src/validators/{domain}.ts` when forms need client validation |
| — | Infer form types: `type X = z.infer<typeof xSchema>` |

### 2.3 Data / business logic hooks

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| `use*RQ` in API files | `useFetch*` for simple list/detail reads (local `useState`) |
| Logic inside modular components or pages | `use*Logic` for multi-step flows, mutations, navigation side effects |
| Sparse `src/hooks/state-hooks/*` | Redux slices + `use*Logic` for cross-screen CRUD |
| React Query cache | Local state **or** Redux — never introduce React Query unless the project already adopts it |

**When to use which (mobile):**

| Situation | Pattern | Examples already in app |
|---|---|---|
| One-shot / screen-local list or detail | `useFetch*` → service | hotels, locations, tour spots |
| Multi-screen shared CRUD / form draft | Redux slice + `use*Logic` | tourBuilder, tripPlanner, packageBooking, community |
| Single submit action with little shared state | `use*Logic` + local state | `useBookingLogic`, `usePaymentLogic` |

### 2.4 UI components

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| `src/components/modular-components/{Feature}Module.tsx` | Feature folder: `src/components/{feature}/` |
| `modular-components/dashboard/user/*Section.tsx` | Dashboard screens + `interface/UserDashboard` cards/sections |
| `modular-components/dashboard/service-admin/...` | `src/app/(tabs)/dashboard/service-admin/*` + components |
| Shared atoms (buttons, inputs) | `src/components/ui/` |
| Role shell composition | `src/components/interface/UserDashboard.tsx` / `ServiceAdminDashboard.tsx` |

**What to port from UI:**
- User flows, fields, empty/error states, filters, status rules
- Which API fields are displayed / edited

**What not to port literally:**
- `div` / `span` / CSS modules / `theme-*` web classes
- Parallel-route dashboard slot files (`@user`, `@service_admin`)
- Hash-tab web dashboard chrome — mobile uses Stack screens + cards/navigation

### 2.5 Pages / routes

| Frontend route area | Mobile route area |
|---|---|
| `src/app/(info)/hotels`, tour-spots, … | `(tabs)/explore/` (+ root detail screens) |
| `src/app/booking/*` | Explore booking screens + tracking/dashboard booking detail |
| `src/app/(tour_builder)/*` | Explore tour-* screens (+ optional `(tour-builder)` group) |
| `src/app/community/*` | `(tabs)/community/` |
| `src/app/(shop)/wallet`, payment | Payments via hooks/screens; wallet often stub — check progress file |
| `src/app/dashboard/` + `@user` / `@service_admin` / `@master_admin` / `@employee` | `(tabs)/dashboard/` with role switch in `index.tsx` |
| `src/app/(auth)/*` | `(auth)/login`, `register` |

**Page conversion rule:**
- Frontend `page.tsx` is a thin shell → find the **modular component** it mounts; that is the real source.
- Mobile route file stays thin: call hook(s), render feature components, `router.push` only.

```tsx
// Mobile screen shape (default export only in src/app/**)
export default function SomeScreen() {
  const { items, loading, handlers } = useSomeLogic();
  return <SomeFeatureList items={items} loading={loading} {...handlers} />;
}
```

### 2.6 State (Redux)

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| Auth + some global Redux | `authSlice` always |
| React Query for server cache | Slice only when domain is multi-screen CRUD |
| — | Register new slices in `src/store/store.ts` |

Do **not** create a slice for every ported module. Prefer `useFetch*` first.

### 2.7 Styling conversion

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| `theme-section`, `theme-btn-teal`, CSS vars | NativeWind tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-text`, …) + `dark:` |
| Multi brand themes (`forest` / `dusk` / …) | Light/dark via `useTheme()` — do not port all web themes |
| Responsive `md:` / `lg:` grids | Flex column, `FlatList`, mobile spacing from `theme.spacing` |
| Hover states | `Pressable` / `active:opacity-75` |

Never hardcode hex — use `tailwind.config.js` / `src/constants/theme.ts`.
Every color class needs a `dark:` counterpart (or `isDark` + token).

### 2.8 i18n (mobile-only requirement)

Web may hardcode English. Mobile must not.
1. Add keys to `src/constants/translationKeys.ts`
2. Add strings to `src/locales/en.json` and `src/locales/bn.json`
3. Use `useTranslation()` + `TRANSLATION_KEYS` in UI

