## 4. Workflow: port one module/section

### Step A — Scope from frontend (read-only)

1. Identify the user-facing entry: which `src/app/**/page.tsx`?
2. Open the **modular component(s)** that page renders (not only the page shell).
3. List every `*Api.use*RQ` / mutation used (endpoints + payloads).
4. Note role gates (`SERVICE_ADMIN`, master-admin, service type switches).
5. Note status rules (e.g. cannot edit `CONFIRMED` bookings).
6. Check `app-integration-progress.mdc` — skip work that is already Done; prefer listed priorities.

### Step B — API parity on mobile

1. Confirm backend route exists and matches frontend paths.
2. Implement/extend mobile service functions; keep names aligned with existing mobile style (`fetchX`, `getX`, `createX`).
3. Manually verify unwrap shape against a real response if unsure (`data` vs nested `results`).

### Step C — Hook layer

1. Read-only list/detail → `useFetch*` with `loading` / error (`Alert` or `error` string — match sibling hooks).
2. Mutations + shared lists → slice thunks + `use*Logic`.
3. Never call `getApiInstance()` from a screen; always service → hook → screen.

### Step D — UI rebuild (not copy-paste)

1. Rebuild layout with RN primitives (`View`, `Text`, `Pressable`, `FlatList`, `Modal`).
2. Reuse `src/components/ui/*` before inventing new primitives.
3. Match mobile visual language (existing cards, spacing, elevation), not web card chrome.
4. Support light/dark + EN/BN from the first PR of that screen.

### Step E — Route & navigation

1. Add kebab-case screen files under the correct group.
2. Register in that group’s `_layout.tsx` if using explicit Stack screens.
3. Wire entry points (dashboard `AdminCard`, explore list item, tracking tab, etc.).
4. Use `router.push` / `href` patterns already used in that group.

### Step F — Role & safety

1. Admin-only UI → `useAuthWithAdminCheck()` (or existing dashboard role switch).
2. Do not trust client-only role checks for security; still call protected APIs.
3. No secrets/URLs hardcoded — `API_BASE_URL` from `@/constants/api`.

### Step G — Done criteria

- [ ] Endpoints covered for the scoped UX (not necessarily entire frontend module)
- [ ] Thin screens; logic in hooks
- [ ] Types in `src/types/`
- [ ] Empty + error states handled
- [ ] i18n EN + BN
- [ ] Dark mode
- [ ] No React Query / DOM leftovers
- [ ] `app-integration-progress.mdc` updated

