## 5. Dashboard-specific mapping

Frontend dashboard uses **parallel routes** and large role modules. Mobile uses **one tab** and Stack screens.

| Frontend | Mobile |
|---|---|
| `app/dashboard/@user/page.tsx` + `UserActivityHistoryModule` | `dashboard/index.tsx` → `UserDashboard` + screens (`user-bookings`, `package-bookings`, …) |
| `BookedHotelsSection` / history sections | Dedicated stack screens + cards (`BookingCard`, etc.) |
| `@service_admin` + `HotelServiceAdminModule` tabs | `dashboard/service-admin/*` screens |
| `@master_admin/*ManagerModule` | Not started — new screens under dashboard (or gated section) when prioritized |
| `@employee/*` | Not started |
| Hash/tab sections inside one module | Prefer **separate routes** over giant tabbed web replicas |

**Porting a dashboard section:**
1. Port API + types first.
2. Add a stack screen under `dashboard/` (or `service-admin/`).
3. Add a navigation card/row on `UserDashboard` / `ServiceAdminDashboard`.
4. Extract list/detail components into `components/` — keep screens thin.
5. Reuse `useDashboardLogic` / `useServiceAdminLogic` when the section is booking/hotel admin adjacent; otherwise add a focused hook.

