## 7. Do / Don't

**Do**
- Start from frontend modular-components + `*Api` endpoint list
- Follow the closest existing mobile feature’s folder/hook/slice shape
- Keep screens thin; put orchestration in hooks
- Unwrap API `data` in services
- Update integration progress when a section lands

**Don't**
- Paste JSX with `div`, web-only libraries, or `use*RQ` into the app
- Call Axios/`fetch` from components or screens
- Put business logic in `src/app/**` route files
- Add a Redux slice for simple read-only lists
- Hardcode strings, hex colors, or API base URLs
- Port master-admin/employee chrome unless that role is in scope
- Invent a second API client or React Query layer

---

## 8. Agent shortcut

When the user says “port X from frontend” or “integrate X on mobile”:

1. Read frontend `*Api` + modular component(s) for X  
2. Read mobile sibling feature (tour-builder / hotels / community)  
3. Follow §3 checklist top-to-bottom  
4. Restyle to NativeWind + theme tokens  
5. Wire navigation + i18n  
6. Mark progress in `app-integration-progress.mdc`
